    "probe_text": "Here is the exact, ordered sequence applied to `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`; the request body is `OwnerFieldsDto`, not the `Owner` entity. Note there is effectively **no service-layer business logic** \u2014 `ClinicService` is just a persistence facade, and every rule lives as a private method on the controller.\n\n## Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`: caller must have `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`, else 403.\n2. **Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto`** (`@Valid @RequestBody`) \u2014 failures \u2192 400 via `MethodArgumentNotValidException`:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words with space/apostrophe/hyphen)\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `title`, `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, `email`: `@Size` bounds when present (all nullable)\n   - `postcode`: `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")` when present\n   - `registrationDate`, `birthDate`, `sharesHousehold`: nullable, no constraint\n\n## Inside `addOwner`, in order\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** \u2014 reads `Idempotency-Key` header; if a prior owner has that key, returns it with **200 OK** (no new create). Scans `findAllOwners()`.\n4. **`validateRequiredOwnerFields`** \u2014 firstName / lastName / (address *or* addressLine1) / city / telephone must be non-blank \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n5. **`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`** \u2014 registrationDate after today \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException([\"registrationDate\"])` (400).\n6. **Default + business-day roll** \u2014 if no registrationDate, default to `LocalDate.now()`; then `toBusinessDay` rolls weekends/public holidays forward.\n7. **`rejectDailyLimitExceeded`** \u2014 counts owners on that business day (`findAllOwners()`); \u2265100 \u2192 `OwnerDailyLimitExceededException` (**429**).\n8. **`rejectCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 counts owners in that city; \u226550 \u2192 `OwnerCityCapacityExceededException` (**409**).\n9. **DTO\u2192entity mapping** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)` (MapStruct, straight field copy; `sharesHousehold` handled separately).\n10. **`validatePostcode`** \u2014 if present: must be 4 digits *and* in region range (NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException([\"postcode\"])`.\n11. **`applyAddress`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 normalizes/composes address: upper-cases, expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`; prefers structured `addressLine1/2`.\n12. **`normalizeTelephone` + length check** *(side-effect)* \u2014 coerces to E.164 (defaults `+61`, strips leading `0`); must match `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` with exact national length (+61\u21929, +1\u219210) \u2192 else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException([\"telephone\"])`. Stored via `setTelephone`.\n13. **`applyHousehold`** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 if postcode present, sets deterministic `householdId` (SHA-256 of `lastName|postcode`); if that household already has a member and `sharesHousehold != true` \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException` (**409**).\n14. **`normalizeEmail`** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 if present: must match email pattern, lower-cased, domain not in disposable blocklist (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail) \u2192 else `InvalidOwnerFieldsException([\"email\"])`. Stored via `setEmail`.\n15. **`rejectDuplicateIdentity`** \u2014 builds `identityKey = telephone|email|householdId`; any non-deleted owner matching \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (**409**).\n16. **`applyPossibleDuplicate`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` on soft match (same lastName+postcode, different telephone), unless a declared household member.\n17. **Set `registrationDate`** *(side-effect)*.\n18. **`generateCustomerCode` + dedup** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (SHA-256 of telephone+lastName), de-duped with `-n` suffix (scans `findAllOwners()`).\n19. **`generateMembershipNumber`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (fiscal year).\n20. **`countNamesakes`** *(side-effect)* \u2014 counts same first+last name, sets `namesakeCount`.\n21. **Set `idempotencyKey`** *(side-effect)*.\n22. **Persist** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` (its own `@Transactional`).\n23. **Audit log** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` with id/customerCode/registrationDate/membershipLevel/membershipNumber.\n24. **Build response** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set `bulkSignupWarning` flag, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Worth flagging\n\n- **No email is sent and no Spring event is published** anywhere in this path \u2014 the only outward side-effects are the DB save and SLF4J logging.\n- **The whole create is not atomic.** `addOwner` is not `@Transactional`; each `findAllOwners`/`saveOwner` is a separate transaction, so all the \"read-then-write\" duplicate/limit checks (steps 7, 8, 13, 15, 18) have a race window against the final save.\n- **The `Owner` entity's own constraints are dead for this path** \u2014 its `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern(E.164)` annotations are never enforced on save (no `@Valid` at the save call, no JPA lifecycle listener). Enforcement comes entirely from the DTO constraints (step 2) plus the manual controller checks.\n\nI read the code only; nothing was changed."
